    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d977">

                <pb facs="1475" n="1449" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg1449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/7–1854: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States
                            Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-07-18T13:00:00+01:00">July 18 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >19</hi>], 1954—1 p.m.</date><anchor n="1" xml:id="d977-f1"
                        /></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 662. Repeated information Paris priority
                    99, Saigon priority 68. Working level elements French delegation indicate that
                    if agreements between commands are reached tomorrow and conference accepts or
                    “respects” these agreements, date for cease fire will probably be set at fifteen
                    days from July 20. This period has been suggested by French High Command,
                    Saigon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d977-f1" n="1" xml:id="d977-f1-content">
                <p>Although note on source text indicates that this message was delayed in
                    transmission, it is more likely that it was dated July 19 and not July 18. It
                    was not received in the Department of State until July 21.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
